        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "23 April 1846",
        "text": "You did feel very ill ... now did you not?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7530",
        "messageOrdinal": 375,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-26",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "26 May 1846",
        "text": "I have your parcel—I have your letters ... three letters to-day, it is certainly feast day with me.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8090",
        "messageOrdinal": 400,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-06-12",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "12 June 1846",
        "text": "And to keep all dear to you quite safe and away from all splashing of the mud which we cannot ourselves hope to escape, is the great object,—it does seem to me.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8304",
        "messageOrdinal": 409,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-06-17",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "17 June 1846",
        "text": "So the quaintness passed as quaintness with me.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9816",
        "messageOrdinal": 472,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 July 1846",
        "text": "It is fair that I should.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10133",
        "messageOrdinal": 482,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-08-03",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "3 August 1846",
        "text": "So much for the consent.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s11830",
        "messageOrdinal": 541,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-05",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "5 September 1846",
        "text": "You do ever so much harm by it, observe—you produce catastrophe on catastrophe, just for the sake of my two ears without earrings!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s12258",
        "messageOrdinal": 561,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-09-15",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "15 September 1846",
        "text": "I love him—he is my father—he has good and high qualities after all: he is my father above all.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
